.TH DESKTOP-IDLE-STATUS 1 "October 2026" "Desktop Idle Status 0.1.2"
.SH NAME
desktop-idle-status \- observe KDE Plasma desktop idle blockers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B desktop-idle-status
.RB [ --smoke ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Desktop Idle Status is a session service for the Desktop Idle Status Plasma
system-tray widget. It reports KWin idle inhibitors, screensaver status, lock
and sleep policies, and recent blocking history over the session bus.
.PP
The graphical session starts the packaged systemd user unit. The widget's
Start Service action can also start it explicitly. The service does not load
the native KWin bridge or change desktop settings.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --smoke
Observe for 15 seconds, print a snapshot, and exit. This mode does not acquire
the service bus name or export control methods. Use a separate XDG_DATA_HOME
when diagnosing a session to avoid sharing the daemon's history lock.
.SH FILES
User history and its advisory lock are stored under
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/desktop-idle-status/
(default
.IR ~/.local/share/desktop-idle-status/ ).
Desktop settings are read from the usual KDE user and system configuration
locations and are never rewritten by this service.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR kwriteconfig6 (1)
